---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Research"
  active="research"
  description="Graduate research by Haotian Fu on multimodal sensing, indoor localization, and ADL recognition at Stony Brook University."
>
  <section class="pagehead">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Research</span>
      <h1>Sensing infrastructure, fusion, and generalization.</h1>
      <p>
        Graduate Research Assistant · Stony Brook University · Advisor:
        Prof. Fan Ye (IEEE Fellow) · Sep. 2024 – present
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="project">
        <span class="eyebrow">Mar. 2025 – present</span>
        <h3>Multimodal Dataset Collection, Curation, and Quality Assessment</h3>
        <p class="meta">Home-health monitoring · four-room apartment</p>
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li>
            Led data acquisition and curation for <strong>113 long-duration sessions</strong> of continuous
            activities of daily living (ADLs), integrating <strong>16 UWB sensors</strong> on 16 Raspberry Pis,
            <strong>6 Kinect</strong> video/depth cameras, and <strong>3 wearable</strong> watches/fingertips.
          </li>
          <li>
            Developed and maintained an Android data-collection app and structured protocol with participant
            guidance and timestamped activity annotations for repeatable multimodal recordings.
          </li>
          <li>
            Implemented automated data-quality and metadata workflows to check recording integrity,
            modality availability, and session-level consistency.
          </li>
          <li>
            Mentored undergrad/master’s students in collection, metadata, quality assessment, and Android development.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="project">
        <span class="eyebrow">Nov. 2024 – Feb. 2026</span>
        <h3>Multi-Sensor Fusion for Robust Indoor Human Localization and Tracking (ScoreKFT)</h3>
        <p class="meta">Physics-informed range estimation · particle-filter fusion</p>
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li>
            Identified unreliable range estimation under multipath, occlusion, and clutter as a key obstacle
            to contactless indoor tracking during continuous ADLs.
          </li>
          <li>
            Developed <strong>ScoreKFT</strong>, a physics-informed scoring and particle-filter fusion framework
            over 16 UWB sensors, achieving <strong>0.958 m range RMSE</strong> and over
            <strong>30% lower error</strong> than representative baselines.
          </li>
          <li>
            Built a DBSCAN-based ground-truth pipeline from Kinect video/depth data without prescribed walking paths.
          </li>
          <li>
            Evaluated tracking across <strong>12 long-duration ADL sessions</strong> in a fully furnished apartment.
            First-author paper <strong>accepted</strong> at IEEE GLOBECOM 2026.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p><a class="text-arrow" href="/publications">Publication</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="project">
        <span class="eyebrow">July 2026 – present</span>
        <h3>Cross-Population Generalization for ADL Recognition (ADL-CLIP)</h3>
        <p class="meta">RF–text contrastive learning · GPU clusters</p>
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li>
            Reproduced a Transformer-based RF–text contrastive learning framework with PELT-based temporal
            segmentation and iterative representation refinement for continuous ADL detection.
          </li>
          <li>
            Ran cross-population training and evaluation for an ongoing journal extension on Slurm-managed
            NVIDIA H200/B40 clusters, troubleshooting PyTorch/CUDA environments.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <span class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:28px">Undergraduate</span>
      <h2>Prior work at SJTU</h2>
      <article class="project">
        <h3>Adaptive Video Streaming under Energy Constraints</h3>
        <p class="meta">
          Dept. of Computer Science, SJTU ·
          <a class="inline-link" href="https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/~lijie/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Prof. Jie Li</a>
        </p>
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li>
            Collaborated on multi-agent reinforcement learning for edge-server video streaming under
            long-term energy constraints.
          </li>
          <li>
            Improved the DRL code framework and analyzed activation functions, learning rates, and exploration strategies.
          </li>
          <li>
            Co-authored a paper published at IEEE GLOBECOM 2023 (second author).
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
